  'The mandatory 16-hour foundation for every VTIARA role: values, patient communication, hygiene, consent, privacy and emergencies.', 'Every new hire completes the Common Core first, over 2.5 days (6 + 5.5 + 4.5 hours), before any role training. It gives everyone the same safe, patient-first foundation through classroom sessions, demonstrations, role-play and a short quiz. Its 16 hours are counted inside each role''s total hours.', 'All new hires: therapists, nurses, dermatologists, housekeeping, telecallers, front desk and managers.', array['No prior clinical qualification required','Basic reading comprehension','Attend the academy practical session']::text[], array['Greet and treat patients with the VTIARA standard of courtesy and privacy','Explain, in simple words, what skin and hair are and why hygiene matters','Clean hands correctly at the right moments and use gloves and masks properly','Separate waste into the right colour bin','Handle consent, photos and patient information without breaking privacy','Act correctly in a fainting, allergic reaction or fire emergency']::text[], array['100% attendance','80% or higher on the 20-question knowledge test (16 of 20)','Hand hygiene practical passed']::text[], '{"attendance_pct":100,"knowledge_pct":80,"practical":"Hand hygiene practical passed"}'::jsonb) on conflict (id) do nothing;
