  array['English']::text[], array['academy','blended']::text[], 'Level 1 Certified Therapist', 12, true, true, true,
  'An 8-week, 280-hour programme that turns a trainee into a safe, consistent skin and hair therapist. Nobody works on a patient until the Level 1 exams are passed.', 'Over 8 weeks (16 hours of Common Core plus 264 therapist hours: about 100 classroom and online, 90 hands-on lab and 90 supervised floor work) you learn skin and hair science, consultation support, facials and skin treatments, hair and scalp treatments, device and laser safety, and products and aftercare. Advanced devices need Level 2, and therapists never diagnose, prescribe or change the doctor''s settings.', 'New therapists (skin, hair, facial), and existing therapists for upskilling.', array['12th pass plus beauty or skin diploma, or a fresher passing the aptitude test','Good communication skills','No active skin infection']::text[], array['Analyse skin and scalp, name common conditions and know exactly when to call the doctor','Complete an intake, find contraindications, set honest expectations and document correctly','Perform approved facial and skin treatments safely and consistently','Perform scalp analysis and approved scalp treatments and assist doctor-led hair procedures','Understand device and laser safety and prepare and assist (independent operation needs Level 2)','Give honest product advice and the right aftercare']::text[], array['100% attendance (missed days made up)','80% or higher on both knowledge tests','All practical stations passed with every critical item','Patient-safety check passed (100%)','Logbook minimums completed','Yearly practical and test; case review every quarter']::text[], '{"attendance_pct":100,"knowledge_pct":80,"practical":"All practical stations passed","logbook":true}'::jsonb) on conflict (id) do nothing;
- Skin layers and functions, the skin barrier, skin types
- Fitzpatrick scale (types I-VI) and how each type reacts to sun and procedures', 1) on conflict (id) do nothing;
- Acne and its grades, pigmentation (melasma, post-inflammatory), rosacea, eczema and dermatitis, ageing
- Recognise infections (fungal, bacterial, viral) and refer them
