  array['English']::text[], array['academy','blended']::text[], 'Nursing Level 1 Certified', 12, true, true, true,
  'A 94-hour programme that makes a registered nurse safe and consistent in a VTIARA dermatology and hair clinic: sterility, medicines, emergencies and documentation.', 'Nurses are the clinic''s safety backbone. Over about 2.5 weeks (16 hours of Common Core plus 78 nursing hours) you learn sterilisation and instrument processing, documentation and consent, medication handling, assisting clinic procedures, emergencies including BLS, and patient counselling. You never diagnose, prescribe, or perform a procedure that has not been ordered by the dermatologist.', 'Newly hired staff nurses, and existing nurses for refresher.', array['GNM or B.Sc Nursing','Valid State Nursing Council registration (verified and copied to file)','Hepatitis B vaccination status recorded']::text[], array['Process instruments so every item used on a patient is clean and sterile','Prepare patients and rooms, check consent and contraindication forms, and document correctly','Store, check and handle medicines safely, including the emergency tray','Prepare for and assist dermatologist-ordered procedures','Recognise and manage reactions and emergencies until the doctor arrives','Give aftercare instructions from approved sheets and confirm understanding']::text[], array['100% attendance','80% or higher on the knowledge test','Both practical exams passed with all critical items','Emergency drill passed (100% of critical steps)','Logbook minimums completed','Yearly BLS renewal and re-certification']::text[], '{"attendance_pct":100,"knowledge_pct":80,"practical":"All practical stations passed","emergency_drill":true,"logbook":true}'::jsonb) on conflict (id) do nothing;
- Critical (enter skin or blood), semi-critical, non-critical; what each needs', 1) on conflict (id) do nothing;
- Point-of-use wipe, soak, manual or ultrasonic cleaning, rinse, dry, inspect, pack with indicator, sterilise, store', 2) on conflict (id) do nothing;
- Cycle settings come from the autoclave and instrument manufacturers; chemical indicators in every pack; biological indicator tests as per policy
- Load logs, pack dates, shelf life, storage, recall of failed loads; single-use items are never reprocessed
- Practice: process a tray from dirty to sterile; read and sign a load log', 3) on conflict (id) do nothing;
- Patient chart, vitals, history, allergies, medication orders, procedure notes, aftercare given', 1) on conflict (id) do nothing;
- Written consent for procedures; separate photo consent; minors and guardians
- Incident and near-miss forms; privacy of records and the Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023
- Practice: complete 5 mock charts; spot errors in 3 sample forms', 2) on conflict (id) do nothing;
- Right patient, right drug, right dose, right route, right time, right documentation; check expiry and look-alike names', 1) on conflict (id) do nothing;
- Room temperature items; refrigerator items at 2-8 degrees C with a twice-daily temperature log; report cold chain breaks', 2) on conflict (id) do nothing;
- Topical anaesthetic creams only as ordered, on the specified area, for the time on the product label, then remove
- Emergency tray contents set by the Medical Advisor; weekly check with signed list
- Practice: read 10 orders and catch the errors; tray check', 3) on conflict (id) do nothing;
- Room and tray set-up, patient identification, positioning and skin preparation', 1) on conflict (id) do nothing;
- Assisting peels, microneedling, PRP, mesotherapy and injectables as ordered by the dermatologist
- PRP blood draw and preparation per the device protocol; labelling of tubes', 2) on conflict (id) do nothing;
- Dressings and wound care; post-procedure monitoring; sharps handling
- Practice: set up and assist 10 mock procedures on models; observe 10 real procedures', 3) on conflict (id) do nothing;
- Vital signs and when to call the doctor', 1) on conflict (id) do nothing;
- Adults: call for help, compressions at 100-120 a minute, depth 5-6 cm, 30 compressions to 2 breaths, AED as soon as available', 2) on conflict (id) do nothing;
