- Practice: BLS on a manikin with a certified instructor; two timed mock emergencies', 3) on conflict (id) do nothing;
- Explaining the procedure, what to expect, warning signs, aftercare, follow-up
- Teach-back to confirm understanding
- Practice: counsel 5 mock patients', 1) on conflict (id) do nothing;
Logbook minimums before Level 1: instrument reprocessing cycles 20; procedures assisted 30; charts completed and checked 40; medication checks with a senior nurse 30; emergency drills 2.', 1) on conflict (id) do nothing;

