- Let the patient finish, repeat back the concern, ask one question at a time
- Simple words in English and the local language; no medical jargon; spell out names and numbers', 2) on conflict (id) do nothing;
- Stay calm, apologise for the inconvenience, fix the problem or escalate
- Practice: recorded 1-minute calls, playback and feedback', 3) on conflict (id) do nothing;
- For each common treatment (acne care, pigmentation, hair fall treatments, PRP and mesotherapy, laser hair reduction, anti-ageing facials and peels, dandruff care): what it is, who it may suit, typical sessions, visit time, general downtime', 1) on conflict (id) do nothing;
- The doctor decides after examination; results vary; no guarantees
- Prices and packages: where to find the current approved list', 2) on conflict (id) do nothing;
- Transfer to the nurse or doctor: pregnancy, medicines, reactions, pain, anything about a current treatment
- Practice: explain 5 treatments in 30 seconds each; quiz with a nurse', 3) on conflict (id) do nothing;
- New enquiry, appointment booking, reminder, reschedule and cancellation, follow-up after visit, complaint call', 1) on conflict (id) do nothing;
- Opening, discovery questions, summary, next step and polite closing
- Practice: 15 scripted calls, then unscripted', 2) on conflict (id) do nothing;
- Create and update a lead; required fields; disposition codes; follow-up dates; notes in plain facts', 1) on conflict (id) do nothing;
- Same-day update rule; duplicate checking; no patient data in personal notes or chats
- Practice: 20 entries in the practice CRM; error review', 2) on conflict (id) do nothing;
- Listen, acknowledge, answer with facts, offer the next step (a consultation), never pressure', 1) on conflict (id) do nothing;
- Price, fear, time, ''I will think'', ''another clinic is cheaper'', ''is it safe?''
- Never create false urgency or exaggerated claims
